# pattern-size-literal-limit: a literal Text Pattern whose program is over
# the Script's patternSize is a load error, and one exactly at it loads.
# Counted repetitions count every copy (spec chapter 6, Limits; chapter 8,
# Compiling). With patternSize 50, `<49 digits>` (49 `class digit` and a
# `match`, 50 instructions) loads, and `<50 digits>` (51) doesn't. The
# diagnostic is pinned, and the Script is left unchanged.
#
# The diagnostic is `pattern too large`, at the literal's opening `<`
# (chapter 2, Load-time diagnostics). The oversized literal is in a Reload's
# source, rather than a Script that fails its first Load, so the Group
# still holds the Script at `> vars`.

> load sized identity=9d97697e8d04e2c0c7c9458c372d7a07666a8ad25d326b0211425ee64cc9e2e8

# A LoadError leaves the Script unchanged (chapter 10, Reload).
> reload sized carry=yes source="script variable p = <50 digits>" identity=13529c7c0fb2a8ae1fe36ac2e18cbb39bbb54868a35280e794d8efb282c8ea5e
diag sized code="pattern too large" pos=1:21

> vars
vars sized p=<49 digits>
